          "literatureReview": "Beta thalassemia screening uses red cell indices and HPLC for hemoglobin separation. Microcytic anemia (MCV <80 fL, MCH <27 pg) suggests thalassemia. Elevated Hb A2 (>3.5%) indicates beta thalassemia trait. Hb F elevation suggests delta-beta thalassemia. HPLC quantifies hemoglobin variants. Used for carrier screening and anemia differential diagnosis. False negatives with iron deficiency or recent transfusion. Confirm with molecular testing. Critical for genetic counseling and prenatal diagnosis planning."
